--
dropped the body
--
libstdc++'s C++20 std::pair converting constructor pair(U1&&, U2&&),
guarded by `requires(_S_constructible<_U1, _U2>())' and explicit(bool)
(with --cpp17 the pair uses enable_if instead).  The call to the static
consteval member in the requires-clause is constant-evaluated with the
class's and the member's template arguments
(cpp20_requires_static_call_atom), so the unviable candidates are removed
during overload resolution; before, the selected constructor had no body
and both members of the pair were arbitrary.  std::map's
_M_get_insert_unique_pos constructs such a pair (cpp20_map_basic).
